WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:04.282
Sometimes you would rather ask a question than
hunt through pages.

00:00:04.402 --> 00:00:11.218
In this video you will open OurWater Guru, ask it
about a well, and learn what it can and cannot do.

00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:16.058
On every page of OurWater, look at the bottom
right corner.

00:00:16.178 --> 00:00:20.954
This round button with a sparkle is OurWater
Guru, your water helper.

00:00:21.783 --> 00:00:25.191
Click it, and the helper slides up from the
bottom.

00:00:25.311 --> 00:00:29.655
Your page stays behind it, so you can keep
your numbers in view.

00:00:30.483 --> 00:00:33.435
At the top are the helper's name and a
counter.

00:00:33.555 --> 00:00:37.035
The counter shows how many questions you have
used this month.

00:00:37.155 --> 00:00:39.435
It starts again on the first.

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:43.514
This note says the helper is still being
tested.

00:00:43.634 --> 00:00:47.882
Its answers can be wrong, so double-check
anything important.

00:00:48.683 --> 00:00:51.875
Under the box, a small line says the same.

00:00:51.995 --> 00:00:56.651
For anything about drinking water, ask a lab
or an expert as well.

00:00:57.483 --> 00:01:02.403
Drag this little bar up to make the helper
taller, or down to make it shorter.

00:01:02.523 --> 00:01:05.523
OurWater remembers the size you chose.

00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:08.294
Not sure what to ask?

00:01:08.414 --> 00:01:10.358
Open What can I ask.

00:01:10.478 --> 00:01:14.222
It holds a list of ready-made, suggested
questions.

00:01:15.050 --> 00:01:22.490
There are nine: learn to record, find stations,
explain this screen, compare periods, check data,

00:01:22.610 --> 00:01:27.410
plan visits, add up rain, write a report, and
read a photo.

00:01:28.217 --> 00:01:31.793
Tap one, and its question drops into the box.

00:01:31.913 --> 00:01:35.705
Nothing is sent yet, so you can change the
words first.

00:01:36.517 --> 00:01:40.333
Or type your own question, the way you would
ask a neighbour.

00:01:40.453 --> 00:01:44.029
Here we ask for the water level in Asha's open
well.

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:47.850
Press the round arrow, or the Enter key.

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:52.554
A moment later the answer appears, with the
important numbers in bold.

00:01:53.383 --> 00:01:58.663
It names the well, says when it was last
measured, and how far down the water is.

00:01:58.783 --> 00:02:01.783
A smaller number means closer to the ground.

00:02:02.583 --> 00:02:07.959
Under the answer, a short note reminds you that
these are measurements contributed by users,

00:02:08.079 --> 00:02:10.527
which OurWater has not checked.

00:02:11.350 --> 00:02:15.982
The counter went up by one, because every
answer uses one question.

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:19.942
When they are all used, the box locks until
the first.

00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:23.246
Ask as many questions as you like.

00:02:23.366 --> 00:02:26.534
Now we ask how much rain the rain gauge
caught.

00:02:27.350 --> 00:02:32.390
It adds up the rain for the last thirty days,
from that station's own measurements.

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:35.006
Adding up is a good job to give it.

00:02:35.817 --> 00:02:39.201
So OurWater Guru explains and finds.

00:02:39.321 --> 00:02:45.441
It explains a page, finds your stations, reads your
measurements, and helps you plan and write.

00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:50.666
It cannot see the future, so it will not say
when a well will dry.

00:02:50.786 --> 00:02:53.882
It will not certify water as safe to drink.

00:02:54.683 --> 00:02:57.035
And it never changes your data.

00:02:57.155 --> 00:03:02.675
It can open a page, or fill in a form for you
to check, but only you can press Save.

00:03:03.483 --> 00:03:06.243
Have a photo of a meter or a log book?

00:03:06.363 --> 00:03:09.483
Tap the camera button, and choose the picture.

00:03:10.283 --> 00:03:14.747
Your picture appears above the box, with a
small cross to remove it.

00:03:14.867 --> 00:03:18.707
Ask the helper to read it, then check the
numbers yourself.

00:03:19.517 --> 00:03:21.389
Prefer to talk?

00:03:21.509 --> 00:03:26.909
The speaker button reads answers aloud, and
the wave button starts a hands-free chat.

00:03:27.717 --> 00:03:31.149
The microphone button turns your voice into a
question.

00:03:31.269 --> 00:03:34.893
Your browser or phone asks permission the
first time.

00:03:35.717 --> 00:03:38.501
To start fresh, tap the bin button.

00:03:38.621 --> 00:03:42.653
The conversation is wiped, and your counter
stays as it was.

00:03:43.483 --> 00:03:47.515
Double-click the little bar to bring the
helper back to half the screen.

00:03:48.317 --> 00:03:51.629
When you are done, close the helper with the
cross.

00:03:51.749 --> 00:03:56.141
Your page is right where you left it, and the
button waits for next time.

00:03:56.950 --> 00:04:01.558
Ask OurWater Guru for a quick, plain answer
about your water.

00:04:01.678 --> 00:04:05.662
Check what it tells you, and keep recording
your own measurements.

00:04:05.782 --> 00:04:08.446
Thanks for helping look after our water.
